# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
# xdm chooser "root" icon fixture, built from the guest's own 64-bit command
# words in the retained replay mgras-target-first-rerun-20260921.codex/qemu/
# xsgi-mask-dynamic-0x81.replay (group ROOT, lines 1681546-1681847), plus a
# companion Toolchest cascade-arrow box (group TOOLCHEST, from the separate
# capture irix-20260922T055519-8b72de/qemu.trace, lines 2915440-2915586, the
# same group already covered by wp5/charl-rule/charl-rule.md/charl-rule.replay)
# placed beside it so both halves of the reported defect are in one file. Every
# 'write 8 0x120400' word is the guest's own command word, copied by line
# number from its source, never re-encoded.
#
# Both groups use FILLMODE byte-transfer mode (0x110 bit 23 set), but submit
# different guest-side conventions under it. ROOT: exactly ceil(width/2)
# (state CHAR_H, exec CHAR_L) pairs per row, two indexed pixels per pair
# (pixel0=CHAR_H&0xff, pixel1=CHAR_L&0xff, skip=0) -- confirmed by machine-
# decoding all 128 execs of this group with wp2/decode_replay.py's own
# selector arithmetic: exactly 8 pairs/row x 16 rows, low bytes alternating
# 0xc0/0xc1 by row parity, giving a checkerboard dither pixel(r,c) = 0xc0 if
# (r+c) even else 0xc1. TOOLCHEST: 8 independent bytes per CHAR_L execute,
# row advancing every ceil((skip+w)/8) executes with skip=(row*4*ceil(w/4))%8
# -- the rule already landed to trunk in commit e84435d2a3 ("paint CHAR_H/
# CHAR_L by FILLMODE", verified present in hw/misc/sgi-mgras-raster.c's
# si_draw_byte_row at trunk-qemu HEAD 26214bc227), which post-dates and already
# implements charl-rule.md's independently-derived formula for this exact box.
#
# Register 0x159 (ROOT=0x00000080, TOOLCHEST=0x00008000) is now modelled as
# the guest's own selector between these two byte-transfer conventions --
# si_draw_byte_row in hw/misc/sgi-mgras-raster.c dispatches on it (0x0080 =
# two indexed pixels per CHAR_L execute, 0x8000 = the existing eight-pixel
# path). This discriminator is INFERRED from exactly these two observed
# values, not from an independent datasheet or manual citation; any other
# 0x159 value in byte-transfer mode is LOG_UNIMP and inert. 0x102 (2 in both
# groups) and 0x153/0x158 (both restate (h<<16)|w) were considered and ruled
# out as the selector. See wp5/chooser-icons/chooser-icons.md.
#
# Both groups now PASS on trunk after that change: ROOT via the new two-
# pixel-pair path, TOOLCHEST unchanged via the existing eight-pixel path
# (0x159 == 0x8000 keeps that path, verified by a qtest asserting both
# conventions side by side). Before the change, group ROOT failed exactly as
# described below; group TOOLCHEST already passed.
#
# Pre-fix behaviour (kept for record): the landed eight-pixel formula treated
# each exec as 8 independent columns, so its own row counter advanced 4x too
# fast at width 16 and each visible row showed the registers' stray leading
# 0x00 byte as a near-black column every 4th pixel -- the reported vertical
# hatch.
#
# The 'wid' assertions in both groups below are all 0x0: no CHAR_H/CHAR_L
# execute (byte-transfer or otherwise) writes the WID plane, which only a
# rectangle fill with a nonzero COLORMASKMSBS does (si_draw_fill, triggered
# by a BLOCKXYENDI exec -- see hw/misc/sgi-mgras-raster.c and the sibling
# fixture tests/data/mgras/char-modes.replay, which covers the same
# TOOLCHEST box at the same DRBPOINTERS setup and asserts the same 0x0).
# This file's WID values were originally generated as (DRBPOINTERS >> 16)
# by wp5/chooser-icons/build_root_fixture.py, an assumption never checked
# against char-modes.replay or against si_draw_fill's actual gating; that
# was wrong and has been corrected here.
#
# 'pixels'/'wid' assertions read the raw indexed framebuffer/WID plane
# through the qtest-only x-test-pixel/x-test-wid properties, not through the
# console's colour-mapped display surface (x-test-display-pixel). This
# replay's handshake never loads a CMAP/XMAP, so a --screendump of it (or of
# the already-landed sibling char-modes.replay, checked for comparison) is
# uniform black; that is expected for a whitebox raw-plane fixture and is
# not evidence about on-screen colour, which cmap-xmap-wid.replay covers
# separately.

# --- command-channel handshake, copied from tests/data/mgras/fill.replay ---
read 4 0x008000 0x0
write 4 0x011000 0x0
